<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">24 September in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">5 events that happened on 24 September, from 768 to 1996.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/pepin-the-short" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pepin-the-short.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">768 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,258 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Pepin the Short dies, leaving the Franks to Charlemagne and Carloman</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">King Pepin died at Saint-Denis, dividing his kingdom between his sons Charles and Carloman, who were crowned in October. After Carloman's death in 771, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charlemagne">Charlemagne</a> ruled alone.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/carolingian-empire">Carolingian Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pepin-the-short">Pepin the Short</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charlemagne">Charlemagne</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1789">1789 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">237 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Washington signs the Judiciary Act</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Judiciary Act set up the federal court system, fixed the Supreme Court at six justices and created the office of Attorney General. It remains the foundation of the US federal judiciary.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1869">1869 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">157 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Gold price collapses on 'Black Friday'</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Jay Gould and James Fisk's attempt to corner the gold market collapsed when the Grant administration sold Treasury gold. Prices crashed and many speculators were ruined.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1932">1932 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">94 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">B. R. Ambedkar and Hindu leaders sign the Poona Pact</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Agreed with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahatma-gandhi">Gandhi</a> during his fast, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pune">Poona</a> Pact was signed, replacing separate electorates for the 'depressed classes' with reserved seats. Gandhi ended his fast against separate electorates two days later.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1996">1996 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">30 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Comprehensive Nuclear-Test-Ban Treaty opens for signature</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The CTBT, banning all nuclear explosions, opened for signature at the UN and was signed first by President Clinton. It has not entered into force, as key states have not ratified it.</p></div></li></ol>
